Spec: Text Tool

Purpose:
  Create and edit rich text objects on the canvas with full typographic control,
  including multi-line text, character/line spacing, alignment, bending,
  and text-on-path for laser-ready designs.

Owns:
  ./text.ts
  ./text.test.ts

Can modify:
  ../../models/text.ts
  ../../commands/text.ts
  ../../../ui/TextOptionsBar.tsx
  ../../../ui/PropertiesPanel.tsx

Must:
  Click places a text insertion point.
  A hidden textarea captures keyboard input.
  Text renders on canvas in real-time as user types.
  Enter key creates a new line within the same text object.
  Click elsewhere or tool switch commits the text.
  Double-click existing text enters edit mode.
  Empty text is discarded (no empty TextObject in store).
  Text creation uses CreateShapeCommand.
  Event listeners are cleaned up with AbortController (no leaks).
  Escape key finishes editing and commits the text.

Must not:
  Leave orphan textareas in the DOM.
  Commit empty text objects to the store.
  Block global shortcuts while editing (only capture when textarea is focused).
  Store font file data in the project (reference font by name only).

Depends on:
  @BaseTool
  @TextObject
  @CreateShapeCommand
  @opentype.js (for text-to-path conversion and metrics)
  @PathShape (for text-on-path target)

# --- Text Object Properties ---

# These properties are stored on TextObject and editable via TextOptionsBar or Properties panel.

# Typography

# fontFamily: string — system font name
# fontSize: number — height of capital letters in mm
# bold: boolean
# italic: boolean
# upperCase: boolean — force all characters to uppercase for display

# Spacing

# hSpace: number — horizontal character spacing as % of font size (0 = default, positive = wider, negative = tighter)
# vSpace: number — vertical line spacing as % of font height (0 = default / 100% line height)

# Alignment

# alignX: 'left' | 'center' | 'right' — horizontal text anchor
# alignY: 'top' | 'middle' | 'bottom' — vertical text anchor

# Bending

# bend: number — bend radius (0 = no bend, positive = curve upward, negative = curve downward)
# distort: boolean — whether to distort individual characters when bending

# Path attachment

# pathId: string | null — ID of a PathShape to flow text along (null = freestanding)

Exposes:
  TextTool (extends BaseTool)

Scenario: create text
  Given the Text tool is active
  When the user clicks at (200, 150) and types "Hello"
  Then "Hello" appears on canvas at that position
  When the user switches to Select tool
  Then a TextObject with text "Hello" is committed to store

Scenario: multi-line text
  Given the Text tool is active and the user is typing
  When the user presses Enter
  Then a new line is started within the same text object
  And VSpace controls the distance between lines

Scenario: adjust character spacing
  Given a TextObject "LASER" is selected
  When the user sets HSpace to 20 (via TextOptionsBar)
  Then the characters spread apart by 20% of font size
  And the change is undoable

Scenario: bend text into arc
  Given a TextObject "READY" is selected
  When the user drags the bend handle upward
  Then characters arrange along a circular arc curving upward
  And the bend value updates in real time

Scenario: text on path
  Given a TextObject and a PathShape are both selected
  When the user applies "Attach to Path"
  Then the text flows along the path's contour
  And individual characters are positioned tangent to the path
  And the text updates if the path is edited

Scenario: upper case toggle
  Given a TextObject with text "Hello World" is selected
  When the user enables Upper Case in TextOptionsBar
  Then the canvas displays "HELLO WORLD"
  And the stored text property remains "Hello World" (non-destructive)

Scenario: auto-weld overlapping characters
  Given a script font TextObject where letters naturally overlap
  When the user enables Weld in TextOptionsBar
  Then overlapping letter outlines are merged via boolean union
  And no internal cut lines remain between touching characters

Scenario: alignment change
  Given a multi-line TextObject is selected
  When the user changes alignX from 'left' to 'center'
  Then all lines center-align relative to the text anchor point
  And the anchor point position does not move

Tasks:
  [x] Click to place text insertion point.
  [x] Hidden textarea for input capture.
  [x] Real-time canvas rendering of typed text.
  [x] Commit on tool switch / click elsewhere.
  [x] Edit existing text on double-click.
  [x] Discard empty text.
  [x] AbortController for listener cleanup.
  [x] Multi-line text support (Enter key inserts newline).
  [x] Horizontal character spacing (hSpace property + rendering).
  [x] Vertical line spacing (vSpace property + rendering).
  [x] Text horizontal alignment (left / center / right).
  [x] Text vertical alignment (top / middle / bottom).
  [x] Upper case display toggle (non-destructive).
  [ ] Bold and italic style rendering with font variant selection.
  [ ] Text bending — circular arc layout with drag handle.
  [ ] Distort toggle for bent text (warp vs. rigid characters).
  [ ] Text on path — flow text along a selected PathShape.
  [ ] Auto-weld overlapping characters (boolean union on rendered outlines).
  [ ] TextOptionsBar UI component (font, size, spacing, alignment, toggles).
  [ ] Undo/redo for all text property changes via commands.

Done when:
  Multi-line text renders with configurable line spacing.
  Character spacing adjusts visually and persists in project file.
  Alignment options reposition text without moving the anchor.
  Bent text arranges characters along a circular arc.
  Text on path flows characters tangent to the path.
  Upper case toggle displays uppercase without modifying stored text.
  All property changes are undoable.
  TextOptionsBar exposes all properties when a TextObject is selected.
